INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_entry` (`ID`, `Kind`, `Zone`, `SortOrder`, `Faction`, `RequiredState`, `Title`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(355700, 0, 3557, 0, 0, 0, 'The Exodar', 'The Exodar was never meant to be a city. It was a dimensional ship, a satellite of Tempest Keep, the fortress the naaru brought to the Netherstorm of Outland. When Prince Kael''thas and his blood elves seized the keep and captured the naaru M''uru, the naaru O''ros barred them from its own section and hid within the vessel. Prophet Velen led a raid to take it and flee in search of allies on Azeroth, but the voyage ended in disaster. The ship came down on the western side of Azuremyst Isle, crashing into the flank of a mountain, and its survivors cannot say why. The draenei made its largest surviving section their capital. Its heart is the round Seat of the Naaru, where O''ros still dwells, and from it branch the Crystal Hall of the shaman, the Vault of Lights where Velen keeps his court, and the busy Trader''s Tier. Elekks wait outside the entrance, and from a dock below the western wall ships sail to Auberdine, the nearest town of the Alliance the draenei have joined.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Exodar (satellite of Tempest Keep, Velen and Nobundo''s raid, blood elf sabotage, crash on the western side of Azuremyst, largest section made the capital, central hall with three wings); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/O''ros (A''dal, M''uru and O''ros brought Tempest Keep to the Netherstorm; Kael''thas captured M''uru; O''ros barred the elves from its section and hid in the satellite; draenei welcomed into the Alliance after meeting the night elves); quest 9552 description (the mountain that the Exodar has crashed into); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Crystal_Hall, Vault_of_Lights, Trader''s_Tier, Seat_of_the_Naaru; quests 9757 and 9632, 9633 (Valaar''s Berth west of the Exodar, boat to Auberdine, the closest Alliance settlement); azuremyst.json 352418 (Elune''s Blessing sails Auberdine to Valaar''s Berth in 3.3.5); DB spawns: Torallius 17584, Aalun 20914 and elekks at the entrance in area 3557; quest 9279 description and reward text (something happened and the Exodar crashed; I don''t know why the Exodar crashed); creature_text 17073 (if I ever find the ones responsible for the crash); quest 9554 description (the accident of your ship falling)'),
(355701, 1, 3557, 1, 1, 0, 'Seat of the Naaru', 'At the center of the Exodar lies the Seat of the Naaru, a great round hall with a shimmer of purple light at its heart. On its lowest level dwells the naaru O''ros. Around the rim open the bank and the auction house, and the city''s peacekeepers greet visitors with the blessings of the naaru. Herald Bran''daan cries the latest news from both continents, from the Plaguelands to Feathermoon Stronghold. Off the spiral ramp of the main entrance, Caregiver Breel keeps the inn called the Exobar. Not all of the ship survived: two artificers stand before a district ruined in the crash, and from time to time the great hull still shudders.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Seat_of_the_Naaru (round central hall, purple flux, O''ros on the lower levels, bank and auction house, general goods and bags, Exobar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Exodar (inn on a sub-level of the main entrance spiral run by Caregiver Breel; Artificers Andren and Drenin before a district destroyed in the crash); npc_text 6957 (Herald Bran''daan: news from both continents); quests 10373 (Plaguelands call to arms) and 7494 (Feathermoon Stronghold); npc_text 9051 (Breel: sit and make yourself comfortable); gossip 7777 (Exodar Peacekeeper: Blessings of the Naaru); DB spawns: O''ros 17538 at z -296 under the hall; bankers and auctioneers; Artificers 18921, 18924 at -3966,-11768; Camera Shaker 18955 x13 (30-90 second camera shakes) in the city; DB: bankers Jaela 18350, Kellag 16710, Ossco 17773 (gossip 7808) at -3919,-11545 in the bank off the Seat; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Seat_of_the_Naaru lists them as residents'),
(355702, 1, 3557, 2, 1, 0, 'The Crystal Hall', 'The Crystal Hall forms the northern wing of the Exodar, a quiet place built around a shining pool known as the Light Blessed Waters. It belongs to the shaman. Farseer Nobundo teaches here with Sulaa, Gurrag and Hobahken, who bid their pupils respect the elements of this world and the balance its spirits keep. Seer Skaltesh, guide to the shaman seeking enlightenment, offers even those on other paths a draught of elemental sapta, and with it they glimpse the many elemental spirits that share the hall unseen. Broken miners work a small cavern of crystal off to one side. Enchanters and jewelcrafters teach their trades nearby.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Crystal_Hall (northern wing, Light Blessed Waters, crystal-mining cavern, scrolls in naaru runes, trainers, Seer Skaltesh and Sapta Sight revealing many elementals); npc_text 9622 (Skaltesh: guide to the shaman seeking enlightenment, even those who follow different paths); smart_scripts 18985 (casts Create Elemental Sapta); npc_text 8785, 8786 (Sulaa: respect the elements, balance of this world''s elemental spirits); DB spawns: Broken Miner 18892 x12 at about -3697,-11537; Nahogg, Thoth, Farii, Nus, Erett, Sixx 21019 with moths'),
(355703, 1, 3557, 3, 1, 0, 'The Vault of Lights', 'The Vault of Lights, the Exodar''s western wing, is a house of the Light and of learning; a spiral walkway climbs from it to a second entrance above Valaar''s Berth. Paladins train with Jol in the glowing Vindicators'' Sanctum; priests gather in the Anchorites'' Sanctum and mages in the Hall of the Mystics. Holographic emitters run a museum of the Burning Legion, naming each servant of the enemy for passing tour groups, down to the eredar, once the draenei''s own noble kinsmen. Prophet Velen keeps to the upper platform under the watch of his guards, the Shield of Velen.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Vault_of_Lights (western wing overlooking Valaar''s Berth, spiral walkway to a second entrance, holographic museum, Vindicators'' Sanctum, Hall of the Mystics, Anchorites'' Sanctum, Velen and battlemasters on the upper platform); quest 10366 description (Vindicators'' Sanctum, a room surrounded by a vibrant glow of light); creature_text 18896 Exodar Holographic Emitter (mo''arg, dreadlord, eredar ''once our noble kinsmen'' and others); smart_scripts 18903 Audrid leading Torias, Tobin, Curzon and Emony on a waypoint tour; DB: gameobject 195141 Portal to Blasted Lands at -4038,-11556 (Hall of the Mystics), no game event; Shield of Velen 20674 x5 beside Velen; Arcanist Nazalia 35601 Wintergrasp Battle-Mage; battlemasters 20118-20120, 20382, 30581, 35027; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Portal_(city) (portals to the Blasted Lands added to all major cities in patch 3.2.0); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Liedel_the_Just and Arcanist_Nazalia (both added in patch 3.2.0, Vault of Lights)'),
(355704, 1, 3557, 4, 1, 0, 'Trader''s Tier', 'The Trader''s Tier, the southern wing of the Exodar, holds most of the city''s craftsmen and merchants. Smiths, engineers, leatherworkers and tailors keep their corners, and vendors sell weapons and armor of every weight. The ship''s stores are thin. Dugiru, the cloth quartermaster, warns that the Exodar''s once vast supply of textiles has dwindled dangerously low, and asks friends of the draenei for donations. Up the stairs lies the Hunters'' Sanctum, where Ganaar passes on what he learned from the furbolgs about caring for beasts. At the top of a ramp, the highest point of the tier, warriors train on the Ring of Arms, where Behomat hands the little salvaged from the wreckage to those most able to use it.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Trader''s_Tier (southern wing, most trainers and vendors, Hunters'' Sanctum up the stairs, Ring of Arms at the top of a ramp, Funaam, Dugiru); npc_text 10072 (Dugiru: once vast supply of textiles dwindled dangerously low, donating cloth); quest 9675 description and reward text (Ganaar in the Traders Tier, learned much from the furbolgs); quest 10350 description and reward text (Warriors'' Terrace at the highest point of the Traders Tier; what was scavenged from the wreckage must go to those most able); DB gameobjects: signposts Hunters'' Sanctum 183866, Ring of Arms 183867, Mining & Smithing, Engineering, Tailoring, Leatherworking & Skinning, Blunt and Bladed Weapons, Plate Armor & Shields'),
(355705, 2, 3557, 1, 1, 0, 'Prophet Velen', 'Prophet Velen leads the draenei. On Argus he ruled the eredar beside Kil''jaeden and Archimonde, and when Sargeras offered them power, a vision showed Velen the price: worlds destroyed and his people turned to demons. He fled with those who would follow, and the Burning Legion has hunted the draenei ever since and found them even on Draenor, where the corrupted orcs slaughtered them. Now he holds court in the Vault of Lights. As his people seek this world''s help against the Legion, he reminds them that they must also learn to live peaceably among its peoples. He welcomes the Broken as well, and calls the shamanism they teach critical to the draenei''s future.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Velen (Triumvirate with Kil''jaeden and Archimonde, Sargeras'' offer, vision from the naaru K''ure, flight from Argus, Draenor and the orc genocide, raid on the Exodar); npc_text 8953 (Velen: gain the help of this world''s peoples against the Legion, learn to live peaceably amongst them); quest 9555 description (critical to our future that we learn shamanism from the Broken; they are not evil); quest 9461 log text (Velen at the Vault of Lights)'),
(355706, 2, 3557, 2, 1, 0, 'O''ros', 'O''ros is the naaru who came to Azeroth with the draenei and dwells deep in the Seat of the Naaru. With A''dal and M''uru it brought Tempest Keep to the Netherstorm. When Kael''thas Sunstrider''s blood elves took the keep and captured M''uru, O''ros barred them from its own section and hid within the vessel that became the Exodar. The draenei hold it dear enough that one exarch swears by its beardless, geometric head.', 'warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/O''ros (came with A''dal and M''uru, stayed with M''uru at Tempest Keep, barred the elves from its section, hid in the satellite that became the Exodar); quest 9616 reward text (Menelaous: by the beardless, geometric head of O''ros); silvermoon.json 348710 (M''uru held by the blood elves); DB spawn: O''ros 17538 at -3902,-11679, z -296, area 3557'),
(355707, 2, 3557, 3, 1, 0, 'Farseer Nobundo', 'Farseer Nobundo was a vindicator of Draenor until the orcs'' fel magic twisted him into one of the Broken and cut him off from the Light. He went on pilgrimage to learn why and waited decades by an oasis for an answer that never came. Then a wind rose that would not stop, and in its voice he learned the truth: the Light had not forsaken the Broken, and the elements offered another path. When he came home, Velen, who had foreseen it, asked him to lead the Broken and teach shamanism to all. Many still despise the Broken or call the shaman''s way blasphemy; Nobundo asks his pupils not to judge the flame by its outward appearance, nor him.', 'npc_text 9098-9105 (Nobundo''s tale: vindicator, fel energies, Broken cut off from the Light, pilgrimage, oasis, decades, the wind, Velen''s vision, teaching shamanism to all, prejudice and blasphemy); quest 9555 description and reward text (Velen sends the shaman; do not judge the flame for its outward appearance, just as you should not judge mine); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Nobundo (Crystal Hall trainer, first draenei shaman)'),
(355708, 2, 3557, 4, 1, 0, 'Torallius and Aalun', 'Outside the Exodar''s entrance, the elekk pens belong to Torallius the Pack Handler, a one-eyed breeder of the great beasts the draenei brought from Draenor. He trusts no outsider with his elekks until they prove their friendship to his people. When Exarch Menelaous sends him promising youngsters with orders for the front on Bloodmyst Isle, he asks whether this is the best the Hand of Argus can do and swears the newcomer will never make it, then sends them on anyway. Beside him the riding trainer Aalun offers to teach the riding of the finest beasts anyone has seen, for a price, but not to outsiders the draenei do not hold in the highest esteem.', 'quest 9623 description, request and reward text (Menelaous'' orders, Torallius outside the Exodar tending the elekk, adjusts his eyepatch, best we can offer the Hand of Argus); quest 9625 description (you''ll never make it as a Hand of Argus); npc_text 10239 (Torallius: prove your dedication and friendship to our people); npc_text 10705, 10792 (Aalun: exalted with the draenei; finest beasts, enough gold); quest 14082 (Aalun at the entrance to the Exodar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Elekk (native to Draenor, draenei mounts, brought aboard the Exodar); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Torallius_the_Pack_Handler'),
(355709, 2, 3557, 5, 1, 0, 'Huntress Kella Nightbow', 'Huntress Kella Nightbow is a night elf who keeps watch near Valaar''s Berth, west of the Exodar, and every young draenei hunter is sent to her to learn the taming of beasts. Her method comes from the Stillpine furbolgs, who carve totems in the likeness of an animal that let a hunter bond with such a creature for a time. Her pupils begin with the feisty barbed crawlers of the western coast, move on to the greater timberstriders of the north and finish with a nightstalker.', 'quest 9757 description (Kella teaches all eligible hunters to tame beasts; near Valaar''s Berth, west of the Exodar); quests 9591, 9592, 9593 descriptions and reward texts (Stillpine taming totems, barbed crawlers of the western coast, greater timberstriders in the north, nightstalker, unused winged lizard totem); quest 9675 description (Ganaar in the Traders Tier); DB spawn: Kella 17614 at -4269,-11484 by the Boat to Auberdine signpost 181986'),
(355710, 3, 3557, 1, 1, 0, 'The Draenei Call of Water', 'When a draenei shaman has grown in wisdom, Farseer Nobundo calls them back to the Crystal Hall to learn the mysteries of water. A powerful water elemental, Aqueous, has asked for help: something is throwing the waters of Bloodmyst Isle out of balance, and Nobundo is not surprised, given the blood elves'' unnatural ways. With a potion to help them reach her, the shaman finds Aqueous in a hidden reef beneath the waves off the island''s northern shore, where she speaks with them mind to mind. A great disturbance is fouling the waters on and around the isle, plain to see in its creatures. Water gives life, she teaches, yet polluted it brings life to an end, and she would learn how far the harm runs from the essences of her unfortunate sisters, the spirits of the Foul Pool.', 'quests 9500, 9502, 10490 (Sulaa, Farseer Javad in Ironforge, Farseer Umbrua in Stormwind send the shaman to Nobundo); quest 9501 description and reward text (Aqueous, imbalance on Bloodmyst, blood elves'' unnatural predilections, potion, hidden reef off the northern shore, speaking with minds); quests 9503, 9504 (Foul Pool essences of her unfortunate sisters, corruption could spread on ocean currents, pure water sample); quests 9508, 9509 (Tel''athion the Impure''s demented research, destroy the barrels, flask of purest water held back, Nobundo makes the water totem)'),
(355711, 3, 3557, 2, 1, 0, 'The Draenei Call of Air', 'Air is the last of the four elements a draenei shaman comes to know, and Farseer Nobundo calls only those wise enough to go on. He sends them up the Wildwind Path on the northern face of the very mountain the Exodar crashed into. In a cave at its peak lives Velaada, one of his most accomplished pupils, who sees few visitors and heard of this one''s coming on the wind. Air seems ethereal, she teaches, yet fills everything: her cave''s rocks are mostly air, the oceans are saturated with it, and no fire burns without it, though the other elements had best not hear her say so. True wisdom waits with Susurrus, a lord of the winds, at the northern edge of the precipice.', 'quests 9551, 9547, 10491 (Sulaa, Farseer Javad, Farseer Umbrua: the last of the elements); quest 9552 description and reward text (Wildwind Path on the north facing of the mountain the Exodar crashed into, cave at its peak, Velaada one of Nobundo''s most accomplished pupils, whispered on the winds); npc_text 8956 (Velaada: so few visitors up here); quest 9553 description (air permeates everything, rocks mostly air, oceans saturated, fire cannot be sustained, don''t let those elements hear; Susurrus at the northern edge of the precipice); quest 9554 description, request and reward text (no further task, atone for the ship falling from my skies, portion of my being, fly you back down, hair looks ruffled, Nobundo grins, whorl into the air totem); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wildwind_Peak (Susurrus, lord of the air elementals in the region)'),
(355712, 3, 3557, 3, 1, 0, 'Redemption', 'At Azure Watch, the paladin Tullas admits that even he at times struggles to follow the path of the Light, and he sends his best pupils to his own teacher, Jol, in the Vindicators'' Sanctum, a room of the Vault of Lights wrapped in a vibrant glow. Jol''s charge is to set paladins on the way to greater virtue as they devote themselves to the Light and defend their people from every threat. Her first lesson is a tome of divinity, to be studied and understood, for only those who understand what the Light expects of them, and are capable, will attain greater abilities.', 'quest 10366 description and reward text (Tullas: even I struggle; Jol trained me; Vindicators'' Sanctum, a room surrounded by a vibrant glow of light); quest 9598 description and reward text (putting paladins on the path to greater virtue, tome of divinity, acts of compassion in the wake of the crash); quest 9600 description, request and reward text (young Stillpine shaman slaughtered at a Bristlelimb camp after the bridge, Symbol of Life, all life is worth saving if it does not oppose us, bewilderment of the revived); DB: Tullas 17483 at Azure Watch (3576); Young Furbolg Shaman 17542 in Bristlelimb Enclave (3600)');
INSERT INTO `mod_lore_codex_part` (`Entry`, `Part`, `MinState`, `MaxState`, `Body`, `Sources`) VALUES
(355702, 1, 13, 255, 'Of late a new craft has found a place in the hall. Thoth teaches the scribe''s art of inscription beside the other trades, Sessoh keeps the supplies it calls for, and a Lexicon of Power lies open nearby for those who would learn it.', 'DB: Thoth 30716 Inscription Trainer at -3890,-11494 and Sessoh 30732 Inscription Supplies at -3881,-11488, near Seer Skaltesh; gameobject 193981 Lexicon of Power (guid 63176) at -3888,-11498; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Inscription (profession added in patch 3.0.2); mod-individual-progression optional/sql/world/zz_optional_phasing.sql (hides Thoth, Sessoh and Exodar Lexicon 63176 until WotLK)'),
(355703, 1, 8, 255, 'Of late a portal shimmers in the Hall of the Mystics. It opens across the sea onto the Blasted Lands, close by the Dark Portal, and so speeds the Alliance''s travelers on the long road to Outland, the broken remains of Draenor, the world the draenei once called home.', 'DB: gameobject 195141 Portal to Blasted Lands at -4038,-11556 (Hall of the Mystics), no game event; mod-individual-progression data/sql/world/base/ipp_aware_npcs.sql: gameobjects 195141 and 195142 get ScriptName gobject_ipp_tbc, shown from state 8; warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Portal_(city) (portals to the Blasted Lands added to all major cities in patch 3.2.0); npc_text 9098 (Draenor, the remains of which are now known as the Outland)'),
(355703, 2, 13, 255, 'The upper platform now gathers volunteers for war as well. Liedel the Just, a battlemaster near the Prophet''s court, asks who is ready to fight for the Alliance on the battlegrounds, and Arcanist Nazalia, a battle-mage, sends them north into the fight for Wintergrasp Fortress in Northrend, which Alliance and Horde take and lose by turns.', 'DB: Arcanist Nazalia 35601 Wintergrasp Battle-Mage at -3990,-11355 and Liedel the Just 34986 Battlemaster at -3961,-11390, near Velen 17468 at -3994,-11414; neither in game_event_creature; npc_text 14675 (Liedel: are you ready to fight for the Alliance); npc_text 14775, 14777, 14781, 14782 (Nazalia: which faction holds Wintergrasp Fortress, talk to me to enter the battle); warcraft.wiki.gg/wiki/Wintergrasp (Wrath of the Lich King, patch 3.0.2)'),
(355709, 1, 0, 255, 'This pupil learned faster than Kella had imagined. She joked that the timberstrider had not pecked their eyes out, not that she ever thought it would, and once the nightstalker had hunted at their side she put away her last totem, carved in the likeness of a winged lizard she could not even name, and let them tame beasts on their own. Then she sent them to Ganaar in the Trader''s Tier.', 'quest 9592 reward text (the timberstrider didn''t peck your eyes out; not that I thought it would); quest 9593 reward text (learned far more quickly than I first imagined; last taming totem not needed, a monstrous lizard with wings; try it on your own now); quest 9675 (offered by Kella after 9593, RewardNextQuest; Ganaar in the Traders Tier)'),
(355710, 1, 0, 255, 'The essences showed the corruption was worse than Aqueous had feared, so potent that, left unchecked, it could spread to the ocean currents and be carried throughout all of Azeroth. Only water of the greatest purity could counter it, and she sent the shaman to gather some.', 'quest 9504 description (worse than I feared, corruption could spread to the ocean currents throughout Azeroth, sample of the purest water)'),
(355710, 2, 0, 255, 'Water parts easily, Aqueous teaches, yet put enough of it together and it becomes an unstoppable force, and she and the shaman are that force, not those who poisoned the isle. She has found the source: a small camp southwest of the Foul Pool, where Tel''athion the Impure carries on demented research whose filth seeps into the island''s water. Pure water poured over his barrels will draw him out.', 'quest 9504 reward text (water parts easily, an unstoppable force, not those that have poisoned Bloodmyst); quest 9508 description (corruption the by-product of demented research, Tel''athion the Impure''s camp southwest of the Foul Pool, destroy his cache of barrels with the pure water to bring him out)'),
(355710, 3, 0, 255, 'Tel''athion fell, and with him the crisis passed. The restoration of the island''s water has begun, and in time, with the other elements, it will heal itself. Aqueous only wishes the blood elves could see that in fouling their surroundings they are killing themselves as well.', 'quest 9508 log text (bring the head of Tel''athion) and reward text (crisis averted, restoration in motion, the water will heal itself, the blood elves killing themselves)'),
(355710, 4, 0, 255, 'Aqueous had held back a little of the pure water, not from doubt but because she knew the shaman would succeed, and gave it to them in a flask to carry back to Nobundo. The elements had already told the farseer of the shaman''s deeds, and he bound the water''s essence into a powerful water totem.', 'quest 9509 description (held back a little of the water, knew you would succeed, flask of pure water, a very powerful water totem), completion and reward text (the elements have spoken of your deeds, combine its essence into your new water totem)'),
(355711, 1, 0, 255, 'Unlike his brothers and sisters of the other elements, Susurrus asked no task. The shaman had done enough, he judged, to atone for the ship that fell to this place from his skies, and already held the wisdom to use air well. He gave a portion of his own being to carry back to Nobundo, and offered to fly the shaman back down to the Exodar.', 'quest 9553 reward text (Susurrus: you come seeking wisdom); quest 9554 description (no further task, atone for the ship falling from my skies, portion of my being, fly you back down to the Exodar)'),
(355711, 2, 0, 255, 'Back in the Crystal Hall, Nobundo grinned at the shaman''s ruffled hair. Proud of a pupil who had persevered where others falter, he took the whorl from Susurrus and shaped it into an air totem, both a focus and a reminder of the bond forged with the elements.', 'quest 9554 completion text (your hair looks ruffled, Nobundo grins knowingly) and reward text (persevered where others falter, imbue the whorl into your air totem, a focus and a reminder)'),
(355712, 1, 0, 255, 'Then comes a test of compassion, for in the wake of the Exodar''s crash there are always people in need of help. Several young Stillpine shaman, allies of the draenei, stumbled on a Bristlelimb camp just past the bridge to Bloodmyst Isle and were slaughtered to the last. With a Symbol of Life the paladin is to raise one of them from death.', 'quest 9598 reward text (tasks in the wake of the Exodar''s crash, acts of compassion, people who need help); quest 9600 description (young Stillpine shaman slaughtered at a Bristlelimb camp after the bridge, Symbol of Life, resurrect one)'),
(355712, 2, 0, 255, 'The young furbolg woke bewildered, as anyone would who returns to the world of the living to find a strange being standing over them. All life is worth saving if it does not oppose us, Jol teaches; only enemies should be laid to rest for good. The power to call back the fallen is the paladin''s from then on.', 'quest 9600 completion text (all life is worth saving, if it does not oppose us) and reward text (bewilderment of the revived, a strange being, you may call upon this power)');
